# A trailing tab in the WebAssembly specification fixture is a COLUMN, not whitespace.
#
# `src/wasm/tests/spec-run-cases.tsv` is six tab-separated columns per row, and 223 of its 2727
# assertion rows end with an empty last column - an `assert_return` whose function returns nothing.
# The tab that delimits it is what makes the row six columns rather than five, so it is data and the
# reader would notice its absence.
#
# `git diff --check` flags it as trailing whitespace, which was invisible while the file changed a
# row at a time and became 223 findings the moment it was regenerated whole (WASM-004).
# This says the file's whitespace is content, so the check stays useful everywhere else.
src/wasm/tests/spec-run-cases.tsv -whitespace
